---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — Brian J. Mueller" description="What www.brianmueller.com collects, what it does not, and the one thing stored in your browser.">
  <section class="wrap stack stack-l">
    <div class="stack stack-m prose legal">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <hr class="rule-short" />
      <p class="small">Last updated: September 18, 2026</p>
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how B:Drive Communications LLC (“we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses, and discloses information when you use www.brianmueller.com (the “Website” or “Service”), and describes your privacy rights and choices.</p>
      <p>By using the Service, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.</p>
      <h2>Interpretation and Definitions</h2>
      <h3>Interpretation</h3>
      <p>Words with initial capitalization have meanings defined below. These definitions apply whether the terms appear in singular or plural.</p>
      <h3>Definitions</h3>
      <ul>
      <li>Company refers to B:Drive Communications LLC.</li>
      <li>Service refers to the Website.</li>
      <li>Website refers to Brian J. Mueller, accessible at <a href="https://www.brianmueller.com">www.brianmueller.com</a>.</li>
      <li>Personal Data means information that identifies or can reasonably be linked to an individual (directly or indirectly).</li>
      <li>Usage Data means information collected automatically when using the Service (e.g., pages visited, approximate location, device/browser info).</li>
      <li>You means the individual using the Service (or an entity on whose behalf the Service is used).</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <h3>Information you provide to us</h3>
      <p>We may collect information you choose to submit through forms or direct contact, such as:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Name</li>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>The content of your message (and any other information you include)</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Information collected automatically (Usage Data)</h3>
      <p>When you browse the Website, we may automatically collect:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>IP address (often used to derive approximate location)</li>
      <li>Device and browser type/settings</li>
      <li>Pages viewed, time spent, referring/exit pages, and interaction data</li>
      <li>A preference you choose on the site — currently only whether you want light or dark mode — stored in your own browser, not sent to us</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Cookies &amp; Analytics</h2>
      <p>This Website sets no cookies at all. What follows is the complete list of what is stored or recorded.</p>
      <h3>What we actually use</h3>
      <ul>
      <li><b>No Google Analytics.</b> We do not use it, and this site sets no advertising or tracking cookie. The earlier Squarespace version of this site did use Google Analytics; that ended with the rebuild.</li>
      <li><b>Cloudflare Web Analytics.</b> Our host, Cloudflare, provides a small counting script that every page loads from <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com</code>. It is the only third-party file this site loads. It reports the page you viewed, the page you arrived from, and how fast the page loaded, back to this site&rsquo;s own address. It sets no cookie and stores nothing in your browser — not local storage, not session storage, nothing — which we verified on the live site rather than taking on trust. It assigns you no identifier and is not shared between websites, so it cannot follow you from here to anywhere else. It does see your IP address, as every request to every website does; Cloudflare derives an approximate country from it and does not pass it to us. What we see is a count of page views, not people. Any content blocker will stop it, and nothing on this site depends on it loading.</li>
      <li><b>Cloudflare server logs.</b> Like any web host, Cloudflare records requests — IP address, time, page, browser — to serve the site and defend it from abuse. Delivery diagnostics are switched on while the new site is being launched, recording the same request information; we read it for errors, not for who you are.</li>
      <li><b>Your theme preference</b>, stored by your own browser under the key <code>theme</code>. It never leaves your device.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For more detail, see our <a href="/cookies-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
      <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>We use information to:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Provide and maintain the Service</li>
      <li>Respond to inquiries and messages you send us</li>
      <li>Monitor and improve website performance, content, and user experience</li>
      <li>Protect the Service (security, fraud prevention, troubleshooting)</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How We Share Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information in the ordinary sense of selling it for money.</p>
      <p>We may share information:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>With the service providers that run the Website — currently Cloudflare, which provides hosting, delivery and the page-view analytics described above. Cloudflare is our only such provider.</li>
      <li>For legal reasons if required to comply with applicable law, regulation, legal process, or governmental request</li>
      <li>To protect rights and safety of the Company, users, or the public (e.g., security incidents)</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Data Retention</h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Messages you send us are retained as long as needed to respond, maintain records, and handle follow-up, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.</li>
      <li>Cloudflare Web Analytics figures and Cloudflare&rsquo;s server logs are retained according to Cloudflare&rsquo;s own retention practices. We do not hold a separate copy of either.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards to protect information. However, no method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.</p>
      <h2>Your Choices</h2>
      <h3>Cookie controls</h3>
      <p>There are no cookies to manage, and no cookie banner, because this Website sets none. Clearing site data in your browser removes the one thing stored there — your saved light or dark preference.</p>
      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>The Cloudflare Web Analytics script described above does not identify you, assign you an identifier, or set a cookie, so there is no account or profile to opt out of. If you would prefer it not to run at all, any content blocker will stop it and the site behaves identically without it.</p>
      <h3>Global Privacy Control</h3>
      <p>Some browsers support Global Privacy Control (GPC) signals. Where required by applicable law, we will treat GPC as a request to opt out of certain data uses (such as “sale” or “sharing” under some state privacy laws).</p>
      <h2>Privacy Rights (U.S. States and Other Regions)</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights such as:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Accessing or requesting a copy of certain personal information</li>
      <li>Requesting correction or deletion of certain personal information</li>
      <li>Opting out of certain processing (where applicable)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To make a request, contact us using the information below. We may need to verify your identity before responding.</p>
      <h2>Children’s Privacy</h2>
      <p>The Service is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information, please contact us and we will take appropriate steps.</p>
      <h2>Links to Other Websites</h2>
      <p>The Service may include links to third-party sites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of those sites. Please review their policies.</p>
      <h2>Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The updated version will be posted on this page with a revised “Last updated” date.</p>
      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions or want to exercise a privacy right, contact us here:</p>
      <p><a href="mailto:brian@b-drive.us">brian@b-drive.us</a>, or through <a href="/contact">the contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
